# Generated SVGs are also hand-edited

The presentation SVGs under `Metapunkt_artVenture/.../TowardsPracticalUtopias_Aug2026/`
are produced by `build/` **and** edited afterwards in Inkscape by the user. A plain
rebuild destroys that work. This has happened before; the user has asked explicitly
that it not happen again.

## Rules

- Never run `build/build_deck.py` or `build/build_sheets.py` with `--force` unless the
  user has been told what will be overwritten and has agreed.
- `document.write_guarded()` refuses to overwrite any output whose SHA-256 no longer
  matches the fingerprint in `_build_stamp.json`, and copies the file to `_backups/`
  first. Do not weaken, bypass or delete that check, the stamp file, or the backups.
- When the guard trips, the correct move is to **diff the backup against the last
  generated version, port the user's change into `build/`, then rebuild**. Do not
  re-apply the change by editing the output SVG, because the next build will lose it
  again.
- Prefer rebuilding only the artefact you are actually changing. A footer change to the
  sheets is no reason to touch the deck.
- Any new writer of a long-lived SVG/PDF artefact in this folder must go through
  `write_guarded`, not `open(path, "w")`.
